BAO PATCH bao-0001 — BaselineFrame OSR NULL-activation guard (fork patch P4)
Source: recovered verbatim from the patched vendor tree (vendor/mozjs/src-js/mozjs/js/src/jit/BaselineFrame.cpp).
  Cross-verified byte-identical across: bao git tracked tree (clean vs HEAD), crates.io
  bao-mozjs-src-js-140.14.0-0, and every materialized /var/cargo-builds/*/out/build/vsrc tree;
  semantics identical to the 0.21.4-era tracked version (git bb313dd1, BCE-20260621-002).
Upstream base: mozjs-140.14.0 — servo/mozjs release tag
  mozjs-source-ee9f2b2aedc3c58347d66ca8d7b9f92ef1df3f53 (SpiderMonkey FIREFOX_140_14_0esr_RELEASE,
  recorded in mozjs-sys/etc/COMMIT). No upstream patch (0002-0045) touches this file.
Semantics (BCE-20260621-002): BaselineJIT OSR entry dereferences cx->activation()->prev() assuming a
  live interpreter activation chain. Under bao (multi-page navigate + later evaluate driven through
  servo's ScriptThread) cx->activation() can be NULL and prev() can be NULL/non-interpreter ->
  deterministic SIGSEGV. Guard bails with false (caller falls back to the interpreter); behavior
  unchanged when a real interpreter activation chain exists. Authorized mozjs source patch
  (2026-06-21 user authorization, limited to BCE-20260621-002).
Replay: paths are SM-tree-relative (-p1). Applied after 0002-0045 by etc/update.py sort order
  (bao- prefix sorts last). Validate: git apply --check --directory=<SM tree> <this file>.

diff --git a/js/src/jit/BaselineFrame.cpp b/js/src/jit/BaselineFrame.cpp
--- a/js/src/jit/BaselineFrame.cpp
+++ b/js/src/jit/BaselineFrame.cpp
@@ -149,7 +149,28 @@
   JSContext* cx =
       fp->script()->runtimeFromMainThread()->mainContextFromOwnThread();
 
-  Activation* interpActivation = cx->activation()->prev();
+  // BAO PATCH (BCE-20260621-002): Guard against NULL `cx->activation()` and a
+  // NULL or non-interpreter `prev()` activation. SpiderMonkey's BaselineJIT OSR
+  // path assumes both `cx->activation()` is non-NULL and the previous
+  // activation on the stack is an interpreter activation. Under bao's
+  // multi-page + navigate + later-`evaluate` workload (driven from C++ via
+  // servo's ScriptThread), `cx->activation()` can be NULL when OSR is entered
+  // from a C++ frame with no live JitActivation pushed, and even when a
+  // JitActivation exists, its `prev()` can be NULL (no interpreter activation
+  // on the stack). Dereferencing either SIGSEGVs deterministically (`Script#NN`
+  // thread in `pagepool_chaos_memory_safety`).
+  // Bail out cleanly (return false → caller falls back to the interpreter)
+  // instead of crashing. This is conservative: when a real interpreter
+  // activation chain exists, behavior is unchanged. Authorized mozjs upstream
+  // patch (2026-06-21 user written authorization, limited to BCE-20260621-002).
+  Activation* currentActivation = cx->activation();
+  if (!currentActivation) {
+    return false;
+  }
+  Activation* interpActivation = currentActivation->prev();
+  if (!interpActivation || !interpActivation->isInterpreter()) {
+    return false;
+  }
   jsbytecode* pc = interpActivation->asInterpreter()->regs().pc;
   MOZ_ASSERT(fp->script()->containsPC(pc));
 
